invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_auth.c
catches: webpki_auth_test
reason: the scheme that selects the SHA-384 signed content is the P-256
  one, so a P-384 leaf's signature is checked over a SHA-256 digest and
  a P-256 leaf's over a SHA-384 one. bin/webpki_auth_test's p384_sha384
  row is the signature a real server writes, and its
  p384_sha256_content row is the one this edit would accept instead.

--- old
    if (scheme == SIGALG_ECDSA_P384_SHA384) {
        sha512 s384;
--- new
    if (scheme == SIGALG_ECDSA_P256_SHA256) {
        sha512 s384;
